611 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 237 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 489.644961 538.617004 745.964969 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure10) /TU (Forest plot showing mean differences in baseline and end measurements between intervention and control groups across multiple studies. Each study's mean difference with 95% confidence intervals is represented by squares for individual studies and diamonds for overall effects. Subgroups are Cases \(Intervention\) and Control \(Placebo\). The weighted average for each subgroup and overall are provided. Heterogeneity is indicated with I-squared values; ninety-nine percent for cases and eighty-seven percent for controls. The plot includes a central vertical line at zero, indicating no difference.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
612 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 237 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 267.425937 538.617004 415.025943 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure11) /TU (Forest plot displaying mean differences for three subgroups: tripeptides, oligopeptides, and polypeptides. Squares represent individual study estimates with corresponding confidence intervals as horizontal lines. Diamonds indicate pooled estimates per subgroup. The overall random effects model shows a mean difference with prediction interval. Heterogeneity and weight percentages are provided for each study and subgroup.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
