631 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 239 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 518.642978 538.617004 745.442981 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure14) /TU (Forest plot showing a meta-analysis of interventions and control groups across four studies: Murad \(2001\), Lee \(2023\), Lin \(2021\), and Kalil \(2018\). The plot includes baseline and end-mean values, mean differences with 95% confidence intervals, and weight percentages for each study. Results are divided into intervention and placebo subgroups. Random effects models assess heterogeneity, with I-squared values and P-values indicated. A prediction interval is also displayed. The overall effect size is visualized by a red diamond.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
632 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 239 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 311.003939 538.617004 456.683932 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure15) /TU (Forest plot showing mean differences between baseline and end mean values for three studies by Lee \(2023\), Lin \(2021\), and Kalil \(2018\) within a polypeptides subgroup. The plot displays confidence intervals and weights, with a random effects model predicting an overall mean difference of 2.88 to 3.66. Heterogeneity is zero percent, indicating limited variability across studies.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
633 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 239 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 103.35599 538.617004 249.035983 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure16) /TU (Forest plot displaying the mean differences between intervention and placebo groups in studies by Taub \(2018\) and Bolke \(2019\). Individual study results are shown with red squares, size indicating study weight, alongside confidence intervals. Random effects models and prediction intervals are illustrated with black diamonds. Heterogeneity statistics are included, with I-squared values and p-values for subgroup differences and overall effect tests.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
