642 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 240 0 R /Rect [ 127.697998 338.68796 467.777985 605.807956 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure17) /TU (Forest plot depicting a meta-analysis of oligopeptides. Two studies are compared: Taub \(2018\) with a baseline-mean difference of 0.99 and an end-mean of 1.01, and Bolke \(2019\) with 35.70 and 44.00, respectively. The mean differences and confidence intervals are shown. Overall, heterogeneity is high with \\\( I^2 = 96\\% \\\). The plot shows a combined mean difference and 95% confidence intervals for each study with weights of 52.2% and 47.8%, respectively.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
643 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 240 0 R /Rect [ 127.697998 177.416964 467.777985 276.536959 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure18) /TU (Forest plot displaying subgroup analysis of oral \(Bolke, 2019\) and topical \(Taub, 2018\) interventions. Oral subgroup has a mean difference of 8.3 with a 95% CI of 4.88 to 11.72, accounting for 47.8% weight. The topical subgroup shows a mean difference of 0.02 with a 95% CI of -0.03 to 0.06, contributing 52.2% weight. Overall mean difference is -4.14 to 12.08 with 100% weight. Random effects model shows high heterogeneity \(I² = 96%\).) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
